    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0366" n="300" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v02/pg300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.51G9/22</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of the American Embassy in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crocker</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Director of
                        the American Bureau of the Japanese Ministry for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Yuki</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-30">December 30, 1940</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Yuki</hi>: At Mr. Terazaki’s request, I
                    am transmitting to you an oral statement, a copy of which I read to him this
                    morning, relating to the question of interference with Red Cross supplies in
                    Indochina.</p>
                <p>Will you please regard this statement as from the American Ambassador to His
                    Excellency, the Minister for Foreign Affairs?</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward S. Crocker</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d215-a1.xml" xpointer="d215-a1"/>
